+# Node 2.1 — Majority vote with qwen7b per-token NLL tie-break
+
+## Score (B_dev)
+
+| selector | diffugpt-m | diffugpt-s | diffullama | dream-base | llada-base | **macro** |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| idea 1.1 (trunk, ar.gpt2.sum) | 0.0000 | 0.0050 | 0.0100 | 0.2350 | 0.4900 | **0.1480** |
+| plain majority (earliest tie-break) | 0.0100 | 0.0150 | 0.0000 | 0.7000 | 0.7450 | **0.2940** |
+| **this node (majority + qwen7b NLL tie-break)** | 0.0100 | 0.0050 | 0.0150 | 0.6750 | 0.7450 | **0.2900** |
+
+Final eval: `score: 0.2900`, correctness PASS, deterministic (2 runs identical),
+0 mismatches between select() and the spec logic on all 1000 dev items.
+
+## Required diagnostics (recomputed, dev, n=200/model)
+
+Per model: (b) tie cases, (c) ties where the NLL rule resolved the tie (picked a
+different answer than plain majority via NLL) vs fell back to earliest-index,
+(d) net +/- items vs plain majority.
+
+| model | (b) tie items | (c) NLL-resolved (answer changed) | (c') NLL changes still wrong / fixed / broke | (d) net vs majority |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| diffugpt-m | 119 | 97 | 97 / 0 / 0 | +0 |
+| diffugpt-s | 120 | 102 | 98 / 1 / 3 | **-2** |
+| diffullama | 148 | 131 | 128 / 3 / 0 | **+3** |
+| dream-base | 39 | 27 | 20 / 1 / **6** | **-5** |
+| llada-base | 23 | 18 | 10 / 4 / **4** | **0** |
+
+Tie items where plain-majority (earliest) answer is wrong: dream 31, llada 18.
+
+## Comparison with coordinator diagnostic
+
+- Coordinator predicted: 23 dream / 13 llada wrong-tie items; NLL fixed 1/14 dream
+  and 4/4 llada; "never broke a tie in the wrong direction" → ~neutral to slightly
+  negative, expecting dream ~0.705, llada ~0.750.
+- Recomputed: fix counts match (dream 1, llada 4), but the "never broke" claim is
+  false on dev: NLL tie-break flipped 6 correct dream and 4 correct llada answers
+  to wrong ones. dream net -5 (0.7000 → 0.6750), llada net 0 (0.7450 → 0.7450).
+- The qwen7b per-token NLL anti-predictiveness that shows up across all candidates
+  also shows up when restricted to tie candidates: on dream it resolves 27 ties but
+  only 1 resolution is correct while 6 flip a correct answer.
+
+## Verdict
+
+Hypothesis (dream >= 0.7000, llada >= 0.7450): **partially met / rejected** —
+llada at floor exactly (0.7450), dream below (0.6750). Macro 0.2900 is slightly
+below plain majority (0.2940) and +0.142 vs trunk (0.1480).
+
+## Changed files
+
+- `solution.py` — select() rewritten: Counter over non-None answers; tied top-count
+  answers broken by min per-token qwen7b NLL (nll_sum/n_tokens) over each answer's
+  usable candidates; unique winner returns its best candidate; remaining ties /
+  all-missing-NLL → earliest candidate index among top-count answers; all-None → 0.
